WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:07.868
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:25.523
Okay, so you don't have
ANYTHING, do you?

00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:28.394
No food, water, guns...

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:32.062
I'll be blunt: you're not selling me
on the "Wait Here" plan.

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:35.911
I'd say that I'd think that this is
going to get worse before it gets better,

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:39.351
but really, I think this is just
going to get worse forever.

00:00:39.351 --> 00:00:42.950
So, in other words, I think it's going
to get worse before it gets worse.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.632
If you bet on that, I think
it's pretty safe money.

00:00:45.632 --> 00:00:45.801
Hah!

00:00:46.014 --> 00:00:46.200
Hah!

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:46.701
Hah!

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:49.499
Okay...

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.934
Hey, there's nothing here, man!

00:00:52.311 --> 00:00:53.921
Except for the tripmine...

00:00:53.921 --> 00:00:57.100
But, y'know, if you don't bother
them, they don't bother you.

00:00:58.603 --> 00:01:00.067
There's no... I...

00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:01.552
I don't...

00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:03.480
What is this?

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.400
Hey, you said take ONE LOOK
out this door, and now...

00:01:08.699 --> 00:01:10.234
I was expecting...

00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:13.000
clowns...?  I don't know.

00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:16.007
He's just trying to trick me.

00:01:16.007 --> 00:01:18.234
LIKE EVERYONE ELSE!

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.601
I should've just shot him.

00:01:21.126 --> 00:01:23.745
Well, he'll be dead soon enough anyway.

00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:26.934
He's the man with the plan
and no food or water.

00:01:28.147 --> 00:01:30.834
Why did they put mines near the ceiling?

00:01:32.115 --> 00:01:36.138
Well, anyway, the "Wait Here"
plan only takes you so far.

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:38.434
In fact, it doesn't take you anywhere.

00:01:39.153 --> 00:01:41.423
It might've been a good plan yesterday.

00:01:41.423 --> 00:01:42.701
Damn, lot of lasers.

00:01:43.528 --> 00:01:45.047
Why is this guy smoking?

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:46.702
Did somebody shoot him in the back?

00:01:46.702 --> 00:01:47.334
IT WAS YOU!

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.406
Okay, another one of you--
okay, stay still.

00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:54.212
Don't move-- no, don't do that--
see, you shouldn't--

00:01:54.212 --> 00:01:54.901
NO!  DON'T J--!

00:01:55.826 --> 00:01:58.601
DON'T YOU EVER DO THAT AGAIN!

00:01:59.221 --> 00:02:01.868
If you don't teach them,
they'll never learn!

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.846
God, that thing almost tripped the laser.

00:02:04.846 --> 00:02:06.914
Why are there so many lasers here?

00:02:06.914 --> 00:02:09.502
I feel like I'm trying to steal a diamond.

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:11.279
Wait, are there diamonds here?

00:02:11.279 --> 00:02:13.500
That would turn my day right around.

00:02:13.987 --> 00:02:16.551
WHOA! Whoa... Not that way.

00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:19.234
That way's a shortcut
to a place I don't want to go.

00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:22.009
[sneezes]

00:02:22.009 --> 00:02:22.947
Yuck.

00:02:22.947 --> 00:02:25.901
Yeah, that's really all I have
to say on the matter.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.134
[lock jiggles]

00:02:28.134 --> 00:02:29.002
Locked...

00:02:29.002 --> 00:02:30.813
Oh, wait, I've been here before.

00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:34.601
This is the door by the
mines and the... pain...

00:02:35.749 --> 00:02:37.883
Jesus! There's rockets in here.

00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:42.358
I wonder they're just the chassis or if
they're totally fueled up next to these mines.

00:02:42.358 --> 00:02:46.393
Hell, knowing us, they're fueled up
and the warheads are still active.

00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:50.006
And we have extra fuel barrels just in case.

00:02:50.006 --> 00:02:53.776
Yeah, wow, look. They just slapped
the mines on everything in sight.

00:02:53.776 --> 00:02:55.703
A loose crate, add a mine.

00:02:55.703 --> 00:02:57.890
Some metal railing, add a mine.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.055
A mop handle, add a mine.

00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:04.410
This room confirms every single thing
I've suspected about the soldiers.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.531
This is their grand strategy
at work, right here.

00:03:07.531 --> 00:03:10.996
Just slapped easily triggered
mines on everything in a room

00:03:10.996 --> 00:03:14.919
that could wipe out half the facility
if there was a chain reaction.

00:03:14.919 --> 00:03:18.945
Oh, and leave some aliens hopping
around in it higgledy-piggledy, too.

00:03:18.945 --> 00:03:21.901
Yeah, there are NO surprises here.

00:03:22.678 --> 00:03:24.868
Just blow up everything in sight.

00:03:25.841 --> 00:03:29.167
Don't worry about how we do
missile research here.

00:03:30.393 --> 00:03:32.500
Now, why is THIS guy smoking?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.200
Does he have any money?

00:03:35.151 --> 00:03:36.025
No...

00:03:36.025 --> 00:03:38.815
I should give the soldiers THAT much credit.

00:03:38.815 --> 00:03:39.567
Where am I?

00:03:40.098 --> 00:03:40.834
Oh.

00:03:42.072 --> 00:03:43.000
What is this?

00:03:43.285 --> 00:03:46.301
It has holes in it like spikes
are gonna come out of it.

00:03:46.301 --> 00:03:48.739
And it has yellow/black caution lines.

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:50.067
Can I trigger it?

00:03:52.157 --> 00:03:54.649
Why would me make something like this?

00:03:54.649 --> 00:03:58.968
Wait, what am I saying? That's the
wrong question to be asking in this place.

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:03.593
Although, it leaves me damned curious what
you would tell other people that it's for.

00:04:03.593 --> 00:04:06.897
I mean it shoots spikes up
out of the ground.

00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:09.204
Do we use it to kill cattle?

00:04:09.204 --> 00:04:11.000
I guess you could-- oh.

00:04:11.923 --> 00:04:14.200
I am NOT... no.

00:04:16.895 --> 00:04:19.579
But, yeah, are they actually
going to kill a cow with that?

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:23.723
That's crazy! It would hit its legs
first and could easily miss its brain.

00:04:23.723 --> 00:04:27.567
It would just make horrible noises
and be in as much pain as possible.

00:04:29.323 --> 00:04:31.567
Okay, so I guess that's why we made it.

00:04:32.036 --> 00:04:33.000
Solved that one.

00:04:35.059 --> 00:04:36.130
I don't get it.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.015
Why did they need this to lift
into the computer room?

00:04:39.015 --> 00:04:40.383
And where are the spikes?

00:04:40.383 --> 00:04:42.120
Are they on a time-delay?

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.267
I better get off this.

00:04:43.903 --> 00:04:45.901
Maybe the spikes haven't
been installed yet.

00:04:46.308 --> 00:04:49.814
I wonder if I can just position one of
these missiles and ride it out of here.

00:04:49.814 --> 00:04:51.801
Nah, I would die on impact.

00:04:52.101 --> 00:04:53.234
All right...

00:04:54.991 --> 00:04:58.167
Guess it's time to check out
what the seizure button does...

00:04:59.656 --> 00:05:00.734
Jeez, that's fast!

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:05.308
Wait a minute, that guy saw all these
mines but he's just hiding in the next room?

00:05:05.308 --> 00:05:06.817
He thinks that's safe?

00:05:06.817 --> 00:05:08.491
Why would anyone think that?

00:05:08.491 --> 00:05:12.332
He should be running from
here as far as he can!

00:05:12.332 --> 00:05:13.868
What is that?!

00:05:14.808 --> 00:05:16.467
Space larva?

00:05:17.851 --> 00:05:20.863
Friggin'... death worm?

00:05:20.863 --> 00:05:22.045
Ehhh...

00:05:22.045 --> 00:05:24.934
Well, it's evil, I know that much, so...

00:05:26.931 --> 00:05:30.567
So, did I kill it?  Or do I need
to take this up a notch?

00:05:31.628 --> 00:05:33.444
No, I think I got it.

00:05:33.444 --> 00:05:34.400
It's dead.

00:05:35.749 --> 00:05:36.076
Dead.

00:05:36.076 --> 00:05:38.383
GUARD: HEEEEY!  AAAAAAAH!

00:05:38.383 --> 00:05:39.701
BLAAAAHHH!

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:40.234
OH!

00:05:45.061 --> 00:05:45.968
WHAT THE FU--!

00:05:48.446 --> 00:05:49.813
Fuckin' dumbass!

00:05:49.813 --> 00:05:51.406
He ran right in front of my sh--

00:05:51.406 --> 00:05:53.106
Jesus Christ!

00:05:53.106 --> 00:05:55.257
See, this is why I don't have friends!

00:05:55.257 --> 00:05:58.669
All they ever do is run around screaming
causing problems for everyone,

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:00.540
until somebody tries to kill them.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.934
Friends are like weeds that scream.

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:05.822
Hey, the lights are on.

00:06:05.822 --> 00:06:09.100
Tell me the keys are in here.
Tell me the keys are in the ignition!

00:06:09.944 --> 00:06:11.034
NO! DAMMIT!

00:06:11.034 --> 00:06:13.067
THAT'S NOT WHAT YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO TELL ME!

00:06:13.423 --> 00:06:14.567
Rrrrrr!

00:06:14.969 --> 00:06:18.617
My lack of preparedness is
biting me in the ass AGAIN!

00:06:18.617 --> 00:06:21.115
I've always meant to learn
how to hotwire a car.

00:06:21.115 --> 00:06:26.730
I never got around to doing it--that crap is
all on the Internet now--there's NO excuse.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:30.000
And let's face it, this is not a
Porsche with a laser-cut key.

00:06:30.614 --> 00:06:34.135
Ah, hell with it. It didn't have
a steering wheel anyway.

00:06:34.135 --> 00:06:36.863
Maybe I should shoot the
tires just out of spite.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:37.275
[turret whines]

00:06:37.275 --> 00:06:37.642
Huh?

00:06:37.642 --> 00:06:39.422
[turret firing]
[screaming]

00:06:39.422 --> 00:06:41.236
[explosions]

00:06:41.236 --> 00:06:43.601
[turret beeping]
MILITARY CAR ALARM!

00:06:47.255 --> 00:06:48.133
[exhales]

00:06:48.517 --> 00:06:52.612
Now, I'm even more pissed about not
being able to hotwire this truck!

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:55.586
It had a turret-gun ready
to fire in the back.

00:06:55.586 --> 00:07:00.191
That's WAY better than those beeping
noises dump trucks make when they back up.

00:07:00.191 --> 00:07:01.831
Okay, I don't see anyone,

00:07:01.831 --> 00:07:05.468
but I'm expecting people dressed
up in full concrete camouflage

00:07:05.468 --> 00:07:07.189
laid flush against the wall.

00:07:07.189 --> 00:07:10.369
I mean, there were fucking ninjas
here last night, weren't there?

00:07:10.369 --> 00:07:11.408
Was that real?

00:07:11.408 --> 00:07:14.491
Of course, now that it's
daytime, they've all disappeared.

00:07:14.491 --> 00:07:18.162
[manta zooms]

00:07:18.162 --> 00:07:20.367
NOT WHAT I WANTED TO SEE!

00:07:25.069 --> 00:07:26.953
[explosions]

00:07:26.953 --> 00:07:27.939
GOOD!

00:07:27.939 --> 00:07:30.300
Exactly as I planned!

00:07:31.044 --> 00:07:31.892
Shit.

00:07:31.892 --> 00:07:33.215
[explosion]

00:07:33.215 --> 00:07:35.739
This was NOT part of the plan!

00:07:35.739 --> 00:07:37.601
YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED TO BE HERE!

00:07:38.196 --> 00:07:39.052
[explosion]

00:07:39.052 --> 00:07:39.767
OH!

00:07:42.338 --> 00:07:44.524
Okay, I know what time it is.

00:07:44.524 --> 00:07:47.725
Because it's clearly rocket launcher time.

00:07:47.725 --> 00:07:49.000
However...

00:07:49.883 --> 00:07:52.029
[explosion]

00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:53.569
Exactly.

00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:58.734
Mr. Dead-to-Rights, the tank operator,
doesn't seem to operate in my time zone.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:02.049
His clock says it's time
to turn me into red paste.

00:08:02.049 --> 00:08:05.534
Okay, time to reflect on
my life choices again.

00:08:07.785 --> 00:08:13.091
That tank totally just shot and killed one
of his soldier buddies without hesitation.

00:08:13.091 --> 00:08:14.683
Almost killed the other one.

00:08:14.683 --> 00:08:17.133
Man, I'm NEVER joining the military.

